cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ATLAS-DIAG: A Low-Cost Digital-Twin-Driven Tester for Pin-Level Stuck-at Fault Diagnosis of 74HCT Logic Chips"
abstract: >-
  ATLAS-DIAG is a low-cost tester for 74HCT00, 02, 04, 08, 32 and 86 logic
  chips built on an STM32 NUCLEO-F446RE. A Python digital twin simulates all
  24 single stuck-at pin faults per chip, compacts the test set with a greedy
  pair-separating search (256 to 3 vectors for the quad gates, 64 to 2 for the
  hex inverter) and exports the tables to the firmware. The board names the
  stuck pin or its equivalence class and confirms every pass with a full
  exhaustive check, standalone with an OLED or from a PC.
